{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01326",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.69,
      "end_seconds": 7.51,
      "duration_seconds": 6.82,
      "text": "Doctor, I've checked them in and done the preliminary measurements, I'll hand them over when you ask."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.07,
      "end_seconds": 14.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "Thanks. Hello, come in, sit down. What brings you in today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 16.11,
      "end_seconds": 21.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.14,
      "end_seconds": 27.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 28.26,
      "end_seconds": 32.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Doctor, it's occasional lightheadedness. That's what we're worried about."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.27,
      "end_seconds": 39.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "When did this begin? I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.95,
      "end_seconds": 43.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Yesterday, it came on out of nowhere."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.56,
      "end_seconds": 47.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Any other symptoms with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.63,
      "end_seconds": 56.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get skipped beats as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.55,
      "end_seconds": 64.11,
      "duration_seconds": 6.56,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 64.21,
      "end_seconds": 70.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.97,
      "text": "tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.67,
      "end_seconds": 78.22,
      "duration_seconds": 6.55,
      "text": "I was getting to that! The skipped beats? That's been for ten days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.69,
      "end_seconds": 82.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Is there something that settles it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.51,
      "end_seconds": 86.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "oh, walking helps a bit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.15,
      "end_seconds": 92.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "Is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.31,
      "end_seconds": 99.87,
      "duration_seconds": 6.56,
      "text": "It's, um... not exactly... well, hard to explain, I mean—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.74,
      "end_seconds": 107.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.85,
      "text": "Let me put it another way: how many times in a typical day or week?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.55,
      "end_seconds": 113.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "I'd say once or twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.57,
      "end_seconds": 119.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "Have you had occasional lightheadedness before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.75,
      "end_seconds": 128.2,
      "duration_seconds": 7.45,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened last winter, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.18,
      "end_seconds": 134.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "A few quick ones: breathlessness, fainting or family history of sudden death?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.9,
      "end_seconds": 150.81,
      "duration_seconds": 14.91,
      "text": "No, no breathlessness, no fainting, no family history of sudden death. I did have poor sleep at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.58,
      "end_seconds": 159.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "right, a few quick ones: energy drinks, leg swelling or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.37,
      "end_seconds": 167.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "No, I'd have said so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.68,
      "end_seconds": 170.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "How's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.04,
      "end_seconds": 173.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.06,
      "text": "Breathing's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.67,
      "end_seconds": 177.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.9,
      "end_seconds": 182.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "That's normal as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.48,
      "end_seconds": 188.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.07,
      "end_seconds": 193.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "I've had an underactive thyroid, yes i've had anxiety, yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.3,
      "end_seconds": 196.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Okay, go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.23,
      "end_seconds": 201.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.83,
      "end_seconds": 206.63,
      "duration_seconds": 0.8,
      "text": "I follow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.83,
      "end_seconds": 212.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "I've had an irregular heartbeat for about ten years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.46,
      "end_seconds": 220.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.83,
      "text": "Alright, anxiety and and high blood pressure, that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.08,
      "end_seconds": 235.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "So, who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.98,
      "end_seconds": 238.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "My partner and our baby"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.34,
      "end_seconds": 244.42,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please. I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 245.9,
      "end_seconds": 248.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "she takes Thyronorm, every morning"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.32,
      "end_seconds": 251.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "how much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 252.41,
      "end_seconds": 256.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "50 micrograms, I think that's what's on the box."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.18,
      "end_seconds": 258.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "Right, right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 259.78,
      "end_seconds": 262.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "She takes escitalopram, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.03,
      "end_seconds": 265.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "how much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 267.21,
      "end_seconds": 286.2,
      "duration_seconds": 18.99,
      "text": "10 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box. She is on valsartan, 80 milligrams, once a day for my blood pressure, I give it to her. She takes bisoprolol, 2.5 milligrams, once a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.75,
      "end_seconds": 287.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "right, right"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 288.99,
      "end_seconds": 295.01,
      "duration_seconds": 6.02,
      "text": "I had apixaban at one point, but I'm off it now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.27,
      "end_seconds": 298.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.0,
      "end_seconds": 304.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Yes, I had an operation for a hernia, last spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.38,
      "end_seconds": 308.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 311.5,
      "end_seconds": 316.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "My grandfather had a stroke. My brother has epilepsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 317.98,
      "end_seconds": 326.58,
      "duration_seconds": 8.6,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Blood pressure 126 over 79, heart rate 83, SpO2 97 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.59,
      "end_seconds": 330.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "good, thank you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.06,
      "end_seconds": 338.13,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.07,
      "end_seconds": 341.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "Breathe out slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 358.24,
      "end_seconds": 361.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "heart sounds are normal with no murmur"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.92,
      "end_seconds": 364.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 378.24,
      "end_seconds": 384.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.52,
      "text": "Pulse is regular at the moment, with a couple of early beats while I listened."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 390.47,
      "end_seconds": 392.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "All finished, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 403.53,
      "end_seconds": 414.1,
      "duration_seconds": 10.57,
      "text": "okay, so my impression is this: I'd lean towards benign extra heartbeats, though we should confirm. A rhythm problem is also on my list"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 416.18,
      "end_seconds": 418.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 419.5,
      "end_seconds": 430.23,
      "duration_seconds": 10.73,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's benign extra heartbeats, though we should confirm, and we'll know more once the an ECG is back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 432.1,
      "end_seconds": 436.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "I've already done an ECG, it's ready for you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 438.02,
      "end_seconds": 452.66,
      "duration_seconds": 14.64,
      "text": "right, thank you try cutting out caffeine for two weeks and see if the beats settle i'd like to see you again after the results are back i think we're done unless you have questions"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 454.49,
      "end_seconds": 456.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 457.61,
      "end_seconds": 458.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
}